An indulgent, cozy potato soup topped like a loaded baked potato. Yukon Gold potatoes are simmered in chicken broth and blended with sour cream and sharp cheddar, then topped with golden, cheese-baked Tater Tots and crispy bacon.

*Adapted from [Food Network Kitchen](https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchen/cheesy-potato-soup-3894914).*

## Ingredients

- 1 pound frozen Tater Tots
- 3 cups shredded sharp cheddar cheese (about 12 ounces, divided)
- 2 tablespoons unsalted butter
- 1 yellow onion, diced (about 1 ½ cups)
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- 2 cloves garlic, minced
- 4 Yukon Gold potatoes, peeled and diced (about 1 ½ pounds)
- 4 cups low-sodium chicken broth
- ¾ cup water (plus up to ¼ cup extra for thinning)
- 2 slices thick-cut bacon, diced
- ½ cup sour cream, divided
- 2 tablespoons chopped fresh chives

## Instructions

1. **Bake the Cheesy Tater Tots:** Preheat your oven to 425°F (220°C). Spread the frozen Tater Tots in a single layer on a rimmed baking sheet. Bake for 20 minutes, tossing halfway through, until deep golden brown and crunchy. Sprinkle 1 cup of the shredded cheddar evenly over the tots and bake for 5 minutes more until the cheese is melted and bubbling. Set aside.
2. **Sauté the Aromatics:** While the tots bake, melt the butter in a large pot or Dutch oven over medium-high heat. Add the diced onion, ¼ teaspoon salt, and a few grinds of black pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and translucent, about 5 minutes. Add the minced garlic and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.
3. **Simmer the Potatoes:** Add the peeled, diced Yukon Gold potatoes, chicken broth, ¾ cup water, and ½ teaspoon salt. Bring to a rolling boil over high heat, then lower heat to maintain a gentle simmer. Cover and cook until potatoes are tender and easily pierced with a fork, 10 to 12 minutes.
4. **Crisp the Bacon:** While the potatoes simmer, cook the diced bacon in a small skillet over medium-high heat until crisp, about 5 minutes. Transfer to paper towels to drain.
5. **Purée and Enrich:** Purée the hot soup directly in the pot using an immersion blender until velvety smooth (add up to ¼ cup extra water if you prefer a lighter texture). Stir in ¼ cup of the sour cream and the remaining 2 cups of cheddar cheese, stirring over low heat until the cheese is fully melted.
6. **Assemble and Serve:** Ladle the hot soup into deep bowls. Pile each bowl with a cluster of the cheesy crispy Tater Tots, a scattering of crisp bacon, a spoonful of the remaining sour cream, and fresh chopped chives. Finish with freshly cracked black pepper.

## Notes

- **Potato Choice:** Yukon Golds produce an exceptionally buttery, creamy texture naturally without needing heavy cream.
- **Tot Crunch:** Keep the cheesy Tater Tots on the baking sheet until right before serving so they stay maximally crunchy when placed on the soup.
